  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: Intransitive godan verb. Xが{慰|なぐさ}む, typically with {心|こころ} or {気|き} as the subject. The transitive pair is {慰|なぐさ}める (to comfort someone).\n\nSomewhat literary; in everyday speech the transitive {慰|なぐさ}める or the noun {慰|なぐさ}め is more common.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {心|こころ}が{慰|なぐさ}む: one's heart is soothed\n- {気|き}が{慰|なぐさ}む: one's feelings are eased\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {慰|なぐさ}める: to comfort someone — the transitive counterpart\n- {癒|い}える: to heal — of a wound or grief mending over time",
